        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>You woke up inside an unfamiliar elevator.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >To escape this apartment building, you must observe your surroundings carefully.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Graffiti inside the elevator, notes stuck to the walls, building notices...<br><strong>Everything could be a clue. Pay close attention to every detail.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Someone—or something—may try to stop you from escaping.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>But don't worry.</strong><br>There are those who genuinely want to help you.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >We hope you'll be able to successfully complete your <strong>Eviction Request Form</strong> and find a way out.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>ExitApartment</strong> is a game inspired by cosmic horror, Japanese &quot;Napolitan&quot; urban legends, dreamcore, and liminal spaces.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Rather than relying on traditional horror or monsters, we focused on evoking fear and unease through bizarre situations and unsettling environments.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Estimated Playtime</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >30–60 minutes</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Option</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Mouse sensitivity, sound volume, brightness, and language settings can be adjusted in the game options.<br><strong>We recommend setting the brightness before starting the game</strong> for the best experience.</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>You woke up inside an unfamiliar elevator.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >To escape this apartment building, you must observe your surroundings carefully.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Graffiti inside the elevator, notes stuck to the walls, building notices...<br><strong>Everything could be a clue. Pay close attention to every detail.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Someone—or something—may try to stop you from escaping.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>But don't worry.</strong><br>There are those who genuinely want to help you.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >We hope you'll be able to successfully complete your <strong>Eviction Request Form</strong> and find a way out.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>ExitApartment</strong> is a game inspired by cosmic horror, Japanese &quot;Napolitan&quot; urban legends, dreamcore, and liminal spaces.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Rather than relying on traditional horror or monsters, we focused on evoking fear and unease through bizarre situations and unsettling environments.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Estimated Playtime</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >30–60 minutes</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Option</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Mouse sensitivity, sound volume, brightness, and language settings can be adjusted in the game options.<br><strong>We recommend setting the brightness before starting the game</strong> for the best experience.</p>",
